---
/**
 * Privacy notice, published after legal review (2026-11-10). The analytics section describes what
 * src/components/Consent.astro actually does; change both together, and update the date at the
 * end. Never state here that the site collects no data: hosting logs process IP addresses.
 *
 * Structure and wording follow Independo's own privacy policy
 * (https://www.independo.app/en/legal/privacy-policy), narrowed to what inderun.dev does.
 */
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { LINKS } from "../site";
import { PRIVACY } from "../seo";

const code =
  "rounded-plate bg-ground-sunk px-[0.32em] py-[0.08em] font-mono text-[0.875em] inset-ring inset-ring-plate-rule";
const list = "mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-ink-muted";
const settings =
  "min-h-10 cursor-pointer rounded-plate border-[1.5px] border-ink bg-transparent px-3.5 py-2 font-semibold text-ink transition-colors duration-160 ease-out-expo hover:bg-ink hover:text-ground [&[hidden]]:hidden";
const independoPrivacy = "https://www.independo.app/en/legal/privacy-policy";
---

<Legal title={PRIVACY.title} description={PRIVACY.description} heading="Privacy notice">

  <p class="mt-6">
    This notice explains which personal data Independo GmbH processes when you visit inderun.dev,
    the website and documentation of the open-source IndeRun SDK, and why. It covers this website
    only; how the SDK itself handles data in the apps that use it is described at the end. For
    everything else Independo does, such as its own products, the
    <a href={independoPrivacy}>Independo privacy policy</a> applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Independo GmbH, Lacknergasse 110/7, 1180 Vienna, Austria.
    Email: <a href="mailto:hello@independo.app">hello@independo.app</a>. Further details are in
    the <a href={LINKS.imprint}>imprint</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    inderun.dev is served by Firebase Hosting, a Google service, through Google's worldwide
    content delivery network. To deliver a page, Google necessarily processes your IP address and
    the request itself: the time, the requested address, the referring page, and the browser and
    operating system your browser reports. Google processes these data on our behalf to deliver
    the website and to keep the service secure and available.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not export these request logs into our own Google project, and we do not combine them
    with other data. The site has no user accounts, forms or comments.
  </p>
  <ul class={list}>
    <li>
      Legal basis: our legitimate interest in delivering the website securely and reliably
      (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </li>
    <li>
      Processor terms: Google processes the data under the Google Cloud Data Processing Addendum,
      which we have accepted for this project (Art. 28 GDPR).
    </li>
    <li>
      Transfers: because pages are delivered from Google's worldwide network, the data may be
      processed outside the European Economic Area, including in the United States. Google LLC is
      certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, and Google's data processing terms include
      the European Commission's standard contractual clauses (Art. 45 and 46 GDPR).
    </li>
    <li>
      Retention: we have no access to these request logs and do not keep copies. Google keeps them
      only as long as it needs them to operate and secure the service.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses Google Analytics 4 (property <code class={code}>G-MZ8Y963XQZ</code>) to count
    which pages are read and how visitors arrive, so we can see what developers need. It works in
    two levels, and the consent banner decides which one applies.
  </p>
  <ul class={list}>
    <li>
      Without your consent (before you choose, and after you decline): Google Analytics sets no
      cookies and sends no identifier that recognises you. Each page view sends a cookieless
      signal: the page address, the referring page, browser and device type, the time, and your
      consent choice. Your IP address reaches Google with the request; Google Analytics 4 uses it
      for an approximate location and does not store it.
    </li>
    <li>
      With your consent: the same data, plus the cookies <code class={code}>_ga</code> and
      <code class={code}>_ga_MZ8Y963XQZ</code>, which hold a pseudonymous identifier to
      distinguish visitors and count returning visits.
    </li>
    <li>
      In both cases advertising storage, ad personalisation and Google signals are switched off.
      We do not send Google names, email addresses or anything you type.
    </li>
    <li>
      Provider: Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, as our
      processor under the Google Ads Data Processing Terms, which we have accepted.
    </li>
    <li>
      Transfers: Google may also process the data in the United States. This rests on the
      European Commission's standard contractual clauses and on Google LLC's certification under
      the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. Despite these safeguards, access by US authorities cannot
      be ruled out entirely.
    </li>
    <li>
      Cookies with your consent rest on that consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR and § 165(3) TKG 2021).
      You can withdraw it at any time, with effect for the future, with “Cookie settings” in the
      footer or with the button below; withdrawing deletes the cookies.
    </li>
    <li>
      The cookieless signals without consent rest on our legitimate interest in knowing which
      pages developers read, so we can improve the documentation (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). They carry
      no cookie and no identifier, so we cannot tell visitors apart or link a signal to you. You
      can object at any time (Art. 21 GDPR). Because we cannot recognise you, the objection has to
      come from your browser: if it sends the Global Privacy Control signal, this site does not
      load Google Analytics at all unless you accept cookies. Google's
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> and
      your browser's tracking protection also block the signals.
    </li>
    <li>
      Retention: the Google Analytics cookies expire after two years at the latest. In the
      property, event-level data is deleted after 2 months, and data tied to the cookie identifier
      after 14 months without a new visit. Reports are built from aggregated data.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <button class={settings} type="button" data-consent-open hidden>Change cookie settings</button>
  </p>

  <h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    Two entries in your browser's local storage keep choices you make on this site; they are
    never sent anywhere: <code class={code}>inderun-consent</code> holds your analytics choice and
    its date (asked again after 12 months), and <code class={code}>starlight-theme</code> holds the
    colour theme you picked. Both are strictly necessary for what you asked for, so they need no
    consent (§ 165(3) TKG 2021). You can delete them at any time in your browser's settings.
  </p>

  <h2>When you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we process your message and your contact details to answer you. This is
    handled like any other request to Independo, as described under “Requests, contacts, and
    customer relationships” in the <a href={independoPrivacy}>Independo privacy policy</a>,
    including the providers involved and how long we keep the data.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    Links to other websites, such as GitHub, npm, Independo and netidee, open services run by
    other operators, and their own privacy notices apply there. Questions, issues and
    contributions to IndeRun are handled on GitHub, under GitHub's terms and privacy statement.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul class={list}>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15),</li>
    <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16),</li>
    <li>have data deleted (Art. 17) or its processing restricted (Art. 18),</li>
    <li>data portability (Art. 20),</li>
    <li>
      object at any time, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to processing based
      on our legitimate interest (Art. 21),
    </li>
    <li>withdraw a consent at any time, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3)).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    An email to <a href="mailto:hello@independo.app">hello@independo.app</a> is enough. You can
    also lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority: in Austria the Datenschutzbehörde,
    Barichgasse 40–42, 1030 Vienna, <a href="mailto:dsb@dsb.gv.at">dsb@dsb.gv.at</a>, or the
    authority where you live or work.
  </p>

  <h2>The IndeRun SDK</h2>
  <p>
    This section is about the SDK, not about this website. IndeRun itself does not send usage
    analytics to Independo. App-configured remote AI providers have their own data handling;
<code class={code}>local_required</code> blocks routing to providers that would send task data out of
    the device. The SDK has no telemetry instrumentation for marketing metrics.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We update this notice when the website or the law changes.
  </p>
  <p>Last updated: 10 November 2026.</p>
</Legal>
